Related: #101586

## What Problem This Solves

Resolves a problem where users with Codex-configured custom `model_providers` cannot route matching OpenClaw provider entries through the native Codex app-server harness. OpenClaw currently accepts only the built-in `codex` and `openai` provider IDs at the Codex harness support gate, so configured proxy, local, or enterprise Codex model providers fall back to the OpenClaw runtime or require local source patches.

## Why This Change Was Made

This adds an advanced `plugins.entries.codex.config.appServer.providerIds` allowlist for the bundled Codex app-server harness, defaulting to the existing `codex` and `openai` behavior. The harness reads the live plugin config during `supports()` so config reloads can change the allowlist before runtime selection; explicit constructor `providerIds` still override this for tests and narrow harness instances.

## User Impact

Operators can now pair a custom OpenClaw provider with `agentRuntime.id: "codex"` and a matching Codex `model_providers` entry, then fail closed if the native Codex app-server cannot run that route. Existing users see no behavior change because the default provider allowlist remains `codex` and `openai`.

Example:

```json5
{
  plugins: {
    entries: {
      codex: {
        enabled: true,
        config: {
          appServer: {
            providerIds: ["codex", "openai", "llm_proxy"]
          }
        }
      }
    }
  },
  models: {
    providers: {
      llm_proxy: {
        agentRuntime: { id: "codex" }
      }
    }
  }
}
```

## Evidence

- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs extensions/codex/src/app-server/config.test.ts extensions/codex/harness.test.ts` → 2 files / 122 tests passed.
- `OPENCLAW_CONFIG_PATH=<temp patched config> OPENCLAW_STATE_DIR=<temp state> LLM_PROXY_API_KEY=<redacted> pnpm openclaw agent --local --json ...` against a configured `llm_proxy/gpt-5.5` route returned the expected smoke reply and reported `provider: "llm_proxy"`, `model: "gpt-5.5"`, `agentHarnessId: "codex"`.
- `pnpm docs:list` completed.
- `git diff --check` completed.
- `pnpm test:extension codex` currently fails on the same 16 tests on both this branch and `origin/main`; sampled failures are existing main-state Codex approval/reviewer expectations, not introduced by this change.
- Upstream Codex source checked locally: `codex-rs/config/src/config_toml.rs` exposes `model_provider` and `model_providers`; `codex-rs/model-provider-info/src/lib.rs` defines custom provider fields including `base_url`, `env_key`, and `wire_api`.

AI-assisted.
